      <td><code>TriggerCustomSound</code> hub method added to <code>PokerHub.cs</code>; base64 audio validated (≤ 700 KB), broadcast to room; <code>CustomSoundTriggered</code> client handler plays audio or shows subtitle; <code>MaximumReceiveMessageSize</code> raised to 1 MB in <code>Program.cs</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>🎰 Suspense Reveal (Group A)</td>
      <td>Slot machine cycling per card (<code>room.js:1408</code>), consensus ordering — majority flips first, outlier last (<code>room.js:1348</code>), supernova for 100% consensus via <code>triggerConsensusSupernova()</code> in <code>celebration.js</code>. All three independently toggleable.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>🃏 Card Back Designs (Group B)</td>
      <td>Four CSS presets: <code>.card-back-baize</code>, <code>.card-back-space</code>, <code>.card-back-retro</code>, seasonal body-class variants. Applied to <code>.participant-badge.voted</code>. Selector in Settings → Appearance. Pure CSS, no external assets.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>🖥️ Presentation Mode + Tab Title (Group D)</td>
      <td>Fullscreen via <code>requestFullscreen()</code> on F key (<code>room.js:676</code>); tab title updates with current story and reveal state (<code>room.js:607,611</code>). Numeric keyboard voting (D3) tracked separately as Group P.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>📝 Story Notes (Group G)</td>
      <td><code>UpdateStoryNotes(storyId, notes)</code> hub method (<code>PokerHub.cs:338</code>); inline textarea per story row; real-time broadcast via <code>StoryNotesUpdated</code>; note shown below story title during estimation.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>🔗 Jira M2 Write-back (Group H)</td>
      <td><code>WriteJiraEstimate</code> hub method (<code>PokerHub.cs:655</code>); auto-called on CompleteStory when Jira key + numeric estimate present; configurable field ID; ✅/❌ icon on story row after PUT.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>🔗 Jira M3 Polish (Group I)</td>
      <td>Description tooltip on Jira key badge; issue type chip (Story/Task); "Open in Jira" ↗ link; JQL pre-fill from saved settings. Wired in <code>_Layout.cshtml</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>🐛 Bug Fixes (Group L)</td>
      <td>L1: all 4 missing test functions (<code>testSpeedBadges</code>, <code>testHotCold</code>, <code>testVoteDist</code>, <code>testDecider</code>) already defined in <code>room.js</code> — no ReferenceErrors. L2: <code>seaConfigModal</code> has no hardcoded <code>aria-hidden</code>. L3: <code>scrollToCards()</code> now flashes a blue outline pulse on the card grid. L4: <code>toggleChat()</code> shows "no one else here yet" toast when alone. L5: stories close button uses correct bottom-sheet close function (<code>_closeStoriesSheet()</code>) and is no longer blue; <code>toggleMobilePanel</code> shows the backdrop. L6: <code>installAppBtn</code> + <code>installApp()</code> already implemented in <code>site.js</code> and navbar.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<hr>

<!-- ═══════════ ARCHIVE ═══════════ -->
<h2 id="archive">Won't Do / Permanently Deferred</h2>

<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Feature</th><th>Reason</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>🔮 Oracle Prediction (v3.0 Group L, v4.0 Group F candidate)</td>
      <td>Fun concept but adds a pre-reveal waiting phase that disrupts the flow for quick sessions. The 10s window feels like friction when the team just wants to see the votes. Removed twice — shelved.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>😈 Devil's Advocate (v3.0 Group N, v4.0 Group G candidate)</td>
      <td>Interesting narrative mechanic but requires server-side secret state per participant, complicates the shame/outlier logic, and can feel unfair to new players who don't know the role exists. Removed twice — shelved.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>📋 Copy estimates to clipboard</td>
      <td>Superseded by Jira write-back (Group H). Teams using Jira get estimates synced automatically; teams not using Jira can manually note estimates in the existing vote history view.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>🔵 Azure DevOps / Linear import</td>
      <td>Same proxy pattern as Jira M1 so technically straightforward, but target user base is Jira-first. Revisit only if there is clear demand from actual users.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>🌡️ Re-vote nudge banner</td>
      <td>Teams already have the hot/cold meter and stats bar showing min/max/average — sufficient signal to self-organise a re-vote discussion. An additional banner would be noise.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>🐉 Boss Fight Arena (v3.0 Group K)</td>
      <td>High complexity state machine, procedural boss art, HP tracking. Fun concept but scope dwarfs value for a planning tool. Revisit only if the app pivots to pure game.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>🔄 Auto-reveal as personal preference</td>
      <td>Confirmed: <code>ToggleAutoReveal</code> has no host check — any participant can toggle it and the checkbox renders for everyone. A personal override would create divergent room state (some participants see manual reveal, others see auto). Won't Do.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>⚙️ Move hardcoded JS limits/timings to appsettings.json</td>
      <td>Server config is for server concerns (DB paths, auth keys, CORS). Client animation timings and thresholds belong in JS/localStorage where users can tune them directly via the settings UI. Won't Do.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>📐 Range Voting (min/max instead of single point)</td>
      <td>Breaking API change to <code>CastVote</code> and all downstream handlers. Disrupts every other feature. Consensus on a range is also harder to act on.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>🗂️ Jira Integration — on-premise / Data Center</td>
      <td>Different auth (OAuth 2.0, Kerberos). Scope creep. Jira Cloud covers the target user base.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

</main>
</div>
</body>
</html>
