    <li>Test: the existing <code>testSpecificSeason(key)</code> function works for custom seasons too</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<!-- GROUP S -->
<div class="group-card" id="group-s">
  <h3>Group S — 🧪 Test Polish</h3>
  <span class="tag">Easy</span><span class="tag">room.js · site.js · _Layout.cshtml</span>

  <h4>S1 — Floor Is Lava: Stop Test Button</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>The 🧪 Test button for Floor Is Lava triggers the animation but provides no way to stop it early</li>
    <li>While the test is running, the button label should change to "⏹ Stop" (with distinct styling)</li>
    <li>Clicking Stop clears the floor-is-lava interval/timeout and restores the room to normal</li>
    <li>Implementation: track a running flag + interval ID in <code>room.js</code>; toggle button text/style; on stop call cleanup logic</li>
    <li>Files: <code>wwwroot/js/room.js</code>, <code>Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml</code></li>
  </ul>

  <h4>S2 — Decider Wheel: Standalone Test with Random Data</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Currently <code>testDecider()</code> in <code>site.js</code> shows "open a room to use this" when no room is active</li>
    <li>Instead, generate fake participant data (3–5 random names) and open the decider wheel with that data</li>
    <li>This allows the wheel to be fully tested from the settings modal on the home page</li>
    <li>Implementation: inject <code>window.roomState = { participants: { ... } }</code> temporarily or call <code>openDecider()</code> with mock data parameter</li>
    <li>Files: <code>wwwroot/js/site.js</code>, <code>wwwroot/js/room.js</code> (openDecider signature)</li>
  </ul>
</div>

