<h2>Extended Gamification Roadmap (from Gemini brainstorm)</h2>

<div class="callout note">
  <strong>Source</strong>
  All ideas in this section originate from the brainstorming session captured in <code>docs/GeminiModel.md</code>. Each feature has been adapted to the existing EstimationStation architecture (vanilla JS, SignalR, in-memory state) and ranked by implementation cost.
</div>

<h3 id="tier-easy">Tier 1 — Quick Wins <span class="effort-pill easy">EASY · 1–3 days each</span></h3>

<div class="feature-tier">
  <div class="feature-tier-header">
    <h3 id="vibe-check" style="margin:0">😊 Anonymous Vibe Check <span class="badge badge-green">#4</span></h3>
    <span class="effort-pill easy">~1 day</span>
  </div>
  <p><b>Concept:</b> Before estimation starts, every participant clicks an emoji representing their mood about the sprint backlog (🚀 excited, 😱 anxious, 😴 bored, 🤔 curious, 😎 confident, 💀 doomed). The room shows an anonymous aggregate as a "weather report" for the facilitator.</p>

  <h4>Backend</h4>
  <pre><code><span class="kw">public async</span> Task <span class="fn">SubmitVibe</span>(<span class="cs">string</span> emoji)
{
    <span class="kw">var</span> room = <span class="fn">CurrentRoom</span>();
    <span class="kw">if</span> (room == <span class="kw">null</span>) <span class="kw">return</span>;
    room.Vibes[Context.ConnectionId] = emoji;
    <span class="kw">await</span> Clients.Group(room.Name).<span class="fn">SendAsync</span>(<span class="str">"VibeUpdated"</span>, room.Vibes.Values.ToList());
}
<span class="kw">public async</span> Task <span class="fn">ResetVibes</span>()
{
    <span class="kw">var</span> room = <span class="fn">CurrentRoom</span>();
    room?.Vibes.Clear();
    <span class="kw">await</span> Clients.Group(room!.Name).<span class="fn">SendAsync</span>(<span class="str">"VibeUpdated"</span>, <span class="kw">new</span> List&lt;<span class="cs">string</span>&gt;());
}</code></pre>

  <h4>Frontend (<code>vibe-check.js</code>)</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Render a small emoji picker above the room when <code>vibeCheckEnabled</code> is on and no votes have been cast yet</li>
    <li>Aggregate received vibes as a row of stacked emoji counts: <code>🚀×3  😱×2  😴×1</code></li>
    <li>Auto-hide once first vote is locked in</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Why Tier 1</h4>
  <p>Single hub method, dictionary on <code>Room</code>, anonymous (no per-user UI state), no animations beyond the existing badge styles. Smallest possible feature.</p>
</div>

<div class="feature-tier">
  <div class="feature-tier-header">
    <h3 id="ghost-mode" style="margin:0">👻 Ghost Mode for Latecomers <span class="badge badge-green">#5</span></h3>
    <span class="effort-pill easy">~1 day</span>
  </div>
  <p><b>Concept:</b> A participant joining mid-ticket (after the first vote is locked but before reveal) joins as a "Ghost." They can see chat/vibes but can't vote until the next ticket. Prevents biased mid-round joins from skewing data.</p>

  <h4>Backend</h4>
  <pre><code><span class="cm">// PokerHub.cs — on JoinRoom, check if any votes already cast for current ticket</span>
<span class="kw">if</span> (room.Participants.Any(p => p.Vote != <span class="kw">null</span>) &amp;&amp; !room.Revealed)
{
    newParticipant.IsGhost = <span class="kw">true</span>;
}

<span class="cm">// On StartNewRound — clear ghost flag for everyone</span>
<span class="kw">public async</span> Task <span class="fn">StartNewRound</span>()
{
    <span class="kw">var</span> room = <span class="fn">CurrentRoom</span>();
    <span class="kw">foreach</span> (<span class="kw">var</span> p <span class="kw">in</span> room.Participants) { p.IsGhost = <span class="kw">false</span>; p.Vote = <span class="kw">null</span>; }
    <span class="kw">await</span> Clients.Group(room.Name).<span class="fn">SendAsync</span>(<span class="str">"NewRoundStarted"</span>, room.Participants);
}</code></pre>

  <h4>Frontend</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>When <code>participant.isGhost === true</code>, disable card-pick buttons and overlay the badge with a translucent 👻 emoji</li>
    <li>Tooltip: "You joined mid-vote — wait for the next round"</li>
    <li>Render their badge at 50% opacity in the participant list</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="feature-tier">
  <div class="feature-tier-header">
    <h3 id="discussion-timer" style="margin:0">☕🌋 Discussion Timer (Coffee &amp; Lava) <span class="badge badge-green">#6</span></h3>
    <span class="effort-pill easy">~2 days</span>
  </div>
  <p><b>Concept:</b> After votes are revealed, start a countdown. If discussion exceeds the configured threshold (default 5 min), one of two overlay effects engages:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Coffee mode (subtle):</b> Steam wisps drift up from the bottom edge; a low-opacity "coffee bean rain" canvas fills the screen at 1% per second. Gentle nudge.</li>
    <li><b>Lava mode (dramatic):</b> Pixel-art lava rises from the bottom at 0.5%/sec. Once it reaches a card or button, that element gets <code>.lava-jump</code> (translateY −30px). Avatars get a hop animation.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Implementation</h4>
  <pre><code><span class="kw">const</span> DEFAULT_DISCUSSION = {
  <span class="op">mode</span>: <span class="str">'off'</span>,            <span class="cm">// 'off' | 'coffee' | 'lava'</span>
  <span class="op">thresholdMs</span>: <span class="num">300_000</span>,
  <span class="op">riseRatePctPerSec</span>: <span class="num">0.5</span>,
  <span class="op">maxOpacity</span>: <span class="num">0.6</span>,
  <span class="op">lavaColor</span>: <span class="str">'#ff5722'</span>,
  <span class="op">steamColor</span>: <span class="str">'rgba(200,200,200,0.6)'</span>
};

<span class="kw">let</span> discussionTimer = <span class="kw">null</span>;
<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">startDiscussionTimer</span>(mode, thresholdMin) {
  <span class="fn">clearTimeout</span>(discussionTimer);
  <span class="kw">if</span> (mode === <span class="str">'off'</span>) <span class="kw">return</span>;
  discussionTimer = <span class="fn">setTimeout</span>(() => <span class="fn">engageOverlay</span>(mode), thresholdMin * <span class="num">60_000</span>);
}
<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">stopDiscussionTimer</span>() { <span class="fn">clearTimeout</span>(discussionTimer); <span class="fn">removeOverlay</span>(); }</code></pre>

  <h4>SignalR Note</h4>
  <p>The Gemini brainstorm calls for <code>EnforceLavaTimer()</code> as a hub method. The lighter-weight approach is to start the timer on every client when <code>VotesRevealed</code> fires and stop it on <code>NewRoundStarted</code> — same wall-clock result, no extra hub traffic.</p>
</div>

<div class="feature-tier">
  <div class="feature-tier-header">
    <h3 id="voice-reveal" style="margin:0">🎤 Voice-Activated Reveal <span class="badge badge-green">#7</span></h3>
    <span class="effort-pill easy">~1 day</span>
  </div>
  <p><b>Concept:</b> Host shouts "REVEAL!" and the cards flip. Uses browser <code>SpeechRecognition</code> API — entirely client-side, no backend changes.</p>

  <pre><code><span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">enableVoiceReveal</span>(phrase = <span class="str">'reveal'</span>) {
  <span class="kw">const</span> SR = window.SpeechRecognition || window.webkitSpeechRecognition;
  <span class="kw">if</span> (!SR) { <span class="fn">showToast</span>(<span class="str">'Voice reveal not supported in this browser'</span>); <span class="kw">return</span>; }
  <span class="kw">const</span> rec = <span class="kw">new</span> SR();
  rec.continuous     = <span class="kw">true</span>;
  rec.interimResults = <span class="kw">false</span>;
  rec.lang           = <span class="str">'en-US'</span>;
  rec.<span class="fn">onresult</span> = (e) => {
    <span class="kw">const</span> t = e.results[e.results.length-<span class="num">1</span>][<span class="num">0</span>].transcript.<span class="fn">toLowerCase</span>().<span class="fn">trim</span>();
    <span class="kw">if</span> (t.<span class="fn">includes</span>(phrase.<span class="fn">toLowerCase</span>())) <span class="fn">triggerRevealAsHost</span>();
  };
  rec.<span class="fn">start</span>();
}</code></pre>

  <p><b>Caveat:</b> Only the host needs to enable it. Display a small 🎤 indicator while listening so users know their mic is open.</p>
</div>

