    <h3 id="boss-fight" style="margin:0">🐉 Boss Fight Arena <span class="badge badge-red">#15</span></h3>
    <span class="effort-pill hard">~2 weeks</span>
  </div>
  <p><b>Concept:</b> When the table is given a high-point ticket (13, 21, 100 — configurable), the room transitions into a "Boss Arena": pixelated dungeon backdrop, the ticket card transforms into a monster sprite with a health bar tied to disagreement. Splitting the ticket shrinks the monster into "minions"; reaching consensus triggers The Finisher.</p>

  <h4>State Machine</h4>
  <pre><code>idle → bossDetected (card with points ≥ threshold)
     → arenaEntered  (backdrop swap, music cue, card morphs into monster)
     → fighting      (health bar = 1 − groupAlignment; updates each reveal)
       ├─ split      (ticket split → monster splits into minions)
       ├─ retreat    (table puts ticket back → monster fades)
       └─ defeated   (consensus → Finisher animation, monster explodes)</code></pre>

  <h4>Why Tier 3</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Requires coupling to the deck/card data model</li>
    <li>Asset-heavy: dungeon backdrop, monster sprites (3+ tiers), minion sprites, music</li>
    <li>State machine has 5 states with multiple transitions to validate</li>
    <li>Health-bar tuning needs play-testing to feel right</li>
  </ul>
