<h2 id="jira">7. Jira Integration <span class="badge badge-orange">Rank #14</span></h2>

<p><b>Concept:</b> Connect to an Atlassian Jira Cloud instance, pull a specific sprint's backlog, filter to stories with no story-points (excluding Bugs/Spikes), and bring them into the EstimationStation deck via a dramatic "Portal Import" animation.</p>

<h3>7.1 Authentication &amp; Configuration</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Per-user Atlassian API token (no passwords). Stored encrypted in <code>appsettings.Local.json</code> or per-room (admin-set)</li>
  <li>Basic Auth with Base64-encoded <code>email:token</code></li>
  <li>Settings UI exposes: Jira domain, email, API token (masked), default board/sprint, custom <code>customfield_*</code> ID for Story Points (defaults to literal <code>"Story Points"</code>)</li>
</ul>

<h3>7.2 JQL</h3>
<pre><code>sprint = {sprintId}
  AND issuetype = "Story"
  AND "Story Points" is EMPTY
<span class="cm">// — or, to widen —</span>
sprint = {sprintId}
  AND issuetype NOT IN ("Bug","Spike","Epic")
  AND "Story Points" is EMPTY</code></pre>

<h3>7.3 C# Service Implementation</h3>
<pre><code><span class="kw">public class</span> <span class="cs">JiraIssueService</span>
{
    <span class="kw">private readonly</span> HttpClient _httpClient;
    <span class="kw">private readonly</span> <span class="cs">string</span> _jiraDomain;
    <span class="kw">private readonly</span> <span class="cs">string</span> _authHeaderValue;
    <span class="kw">private readonly</span> <span class="cs">string</span> _storyPointsField;

    <span class="kw">public</span> <span class="fn">JiraIssueService</span>(HttpClient httpClient, <span class="cs">string</span> email, <span class="cs">string</span> apiToken,
                              <span class="cs">string</span> jiraDomain, <span class="cs">string</span> storyPointsField = <span class="str">"Story Points"</span>)
    {
        _httpClient       = httpClient;
        _jiraDomain       = jiraDomain;
        _storyPointsField = storyPointsField;
        <span class="kw">var</span> credentials  = $<span class="str">"{email}:{apiToken}"</span>;
        _authHeaderValue = Convert.<span class="fn">ToBase64String</span>(Encoding.ASCII.<span class="fn">GetBytes</span>(credentials));
    }

    <span class="kw">public async</span> Task&lt;List&lt;<span class="cs">JiraIssueDto</span>&gt;&gt; <span class="fn">GetUnpointedStoriesAsync</span>(<span class="cs">string</span> sprintId)
    {
        _httpClient.BaseAddress = <span class="kw">new</span> Uri($<span class="str">"https://{_jiraDomain}/"</span>);
        _httpClient.DefaultRequestHeaders.Authorization =
            <span class="kw">new</span> AuthenticationHeaderValue(<span class="str">"Basic"</span>, _authHeaderValue);
        _httpClient.DefaultRequestHeaders.Accept.<span class="fn">Add</span>(
            <span class="kw">new</span> MediaTypeWithQualityHeaderValue(<span class="str">"application/json"</span>));

        <span class="kw">var</span> jql = $<span class="str">"sprint = {sprintId} AND issuetype = 'Story' AND '{_storyPointsField}' is EMPTY"</span>;
        <span class="kw">var</span> fields = <span class="str">"summary,description,issuetype,status"</span>;
        <span class="kw">var</span> url    = $<span class="str">"/rest/api/3/search?jql={Uri.EscapeDataString(jql)}&amp;fields={Uri.EscapeDataString(fields)}"</span>;

        <span class="kw">var</span> response = <span class="kw">await</span> _httpClient.<span class="fn">GetAsync</span>(url);
        <span class="kw">if</span> (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode)
        {
            <span class="kw">var</span> err = <span class="kw">await</span> response.Content.<span class="fn">ReadAsStringAsync</span>();
            <span class="kw">throw new</span> HttpRequestException(
                $<span class="str">"Jira API call failed ({response.StatusCode}): {err}"</span>);
        }

        <span class="kw">var</span> json   = <span class="kw">await</span> response.Content.<span class="fn">ReadAsStringAsync</span>();
        <span class="kw">var</span> result = JsonSerializer.<span class="fn">Deserialize</span>&lt;<span class="cs">JiraSearchResponseDto</span>&gt;(json);
        <span class="kw">return</span> result?.Issues ?? <span class="kw">new</span> List&lt;<span class="cs">JiraIssueDto</span>&gt;();
    }
}

<span class="kw">public class</span> <span class="cs">JiraSearchResponseDto</span> {
    [JsonPropertyName(<span class="str">"issues"</span>)] <span class="kw">public</span> List&lt;<span class="cs">JiraIssueDto</span>&gt; Issues { <span class="kw">get</span>; <span class="kw">set</span>; } = <span class="kw">new</span>();
}
<span class="kw">public class</span> <span class="cs">JiraIssueDto</span> {
    [JsonPropertyName(<span class="str">"id"</span>)]     <span class="kw">public</span> <span class="cs">string</span> Id { <span class="kw">get</span>; <span class="kw">set</span>; } = <span class="str">""</span>;
    [JsonPropertyName(<span class="str">"key"</span>)]    <span class="kw">public</span> <span class="cs">string</span> Key { <span class="kw">get</span>; <span class="kw">set</span>; } = <span class="str">""</span>;
    [JsonPropertyName(<span class="str">"fields"</span>)] <span class="kw">public</span> <span class="cs">IssueFields</span> Fields { <span class="kw">get</span>; <span class="kw">set</span>; } = <span class="kw">new</span>();
}
<span class="kw">public class</span> <span class="cs">IssueFields</span> {
    [JsonPropertyName(<span class="str">"summary"</span>)]     <span class="kw">public</span> <span class="cs">string</span> Summary { <span class="kw">get</span>; <span class="kw">set</span>; } = <span class="str">""</span>;
    [JsonPropertyName(<span class="str">"description"</span>)] <span class="kw">public</span> <span class="cs">object</span>? Description { <span class="kw">get</span>; <span class="kw">set</span>; }  <span class="cm">// ADF object</span>
    [JsonPropertyName(<span class="str">"issuetype"</span>)]   <span class="kw">public</span> <span class="cs">IssueType</span> IssueType { <span class="kw">get</span>; <span class="kw">set</span>; } = <span class="kw">new</span>();
}
<span class="kw">public class</span> <span class="cs">IssueType</span> {
    [JsonPropertyName(<span class="str">"name"</span>)] <span class="kw">public</span> <span class="cs">string</span> Name { <span class="kw">get</span>; <span class="kw">set</span>; } = <span class="str">""</span>;
}</code></pre>

<h3>7.4 Custom-Field Caveat</h3>
<div class="callout warn">
  <strong>Story Points field</strong>
  Many Jira Cloud instances expose Story Points only via a custom field ID (<code>customfield_10016</code> or similar). The service constructor accepts an override. To discover it, the user can open any pointed ticket, append <code>.json</code> to the URL, and Ctrl+F for the value — adjacent key is the custom field ID.
</div>

<h3>7.5 SignalR Broadcast (<code>PokerHub.cs</code>)</h3>
<pre><code><span class="kw">public async</span> Task <span class="fn">ImportFromJira</span>(<span class="cs">string</span> sprintId)
{
    <span class="kw">var</span> issues = <span class="kw">await</span> _jiraService.<span class="fn">GetUnpointedStoriesAsync</span>(sprintId);
    <span class="kw">var</span> roomName = <span class="fn">CurrentRoomName</span>();
    <span class="kw">await</span> Clients.Group(roomName).<span class="fn">SendAsync</span>(<span class="str">"JiraImportStarted"</span>, issues.Count);
    <span class="kw">foreach</span> (<span class="kw">var</span> issue <span class="kw">in</span> issues)
    {
        <span class="kw">await</span> Task.<span class="fn">Delay</span>(<span class="num">120</span>);  <span class="cm">// stagger for portal animation</span>
        <span class="kw">await</span> Clients.Group(roomName).<span class="fn">SendAsync</span>(<span class="str">"JiraIssueArrived"</span>, issue);
    }
    <span class="kw">await</span> Clients.Group(roomName).<span class="fn">SendAsync</span>(<span class="str">"JiraImportCompleted"</span>);
}</code></pre>

<h3>7.6 Portal Import Animation</h3>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><b>Portal opens:</b> Jira-blue swirling vortex (canvas-based, 1.2s ease-out scale-in) appears center-stage</li>
  <li><b>Vacuum effect:</b> Each <code>JiraIssueArrived</code> event spawns a card flying out of the vortex on a parabolic path to its slot in the deck</li>
  <li><b>Dust-off:</b> Imported cards have a sepia + 0.4 brightness CSS filter ("dusty"); class is removed when first vote is locked, accompanied by a 200ms CSS shake to symbolize "awakening"</li>
  <li><b>Portal closes:</b> <code>JiraImportCompleted</code> triggers reverse animation; vortex collapses to a point and fades</li>
</ol>

