<h2 id="bugs">🐛 Bugs — Fix First</h2>

<div class="group-card bug" id="group-t">
  <h3>Group T — 🐛 Bug Fixes <span class="new-tag">new</span> <span class="done-tag">✅ All Done</span></h3>
  <span class="tag">Fix First</span><span class="tag">voice.js · awards.js · seasonal.js · celebration.js · room.js</span>

  <h4 style="margin-top:14px;">T1 — Voice Recognition: InvalidStateError + No Way to Stop <span class="done-tag">✅</span></h4>
  <p>When the user tries to change the voice reveal code while recognition is running, <code>voice.js:73</code> throws <code>InvalidStateError: recognition has already started</code>. Additionally there is no UI to stop listening — the user must reload.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Guard all <code>_voiceRecog.start()</code> calls with a check that recognition is not already started (track with <code>_voiceStarted</code> flag; set on <code>onstart</code>, clear on <code>onend</code>)</li>
    <li>Stop recognition, update the reveal code, then restart to handle in-flight changes</li>
    <li>Click the microphone icon/badge in the navbar to toggle listening mode on/off — same as a mute button</li>
    <li>Microphone icon should clearly indicate active-listening state (pulsing green) vs off (grey)</li>
    <li>File: <code>wwwroot/js/voice.js</code>, <code>Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml</code></li>
  </ul>

  <h4>T2 — Session Awards Shows "Unknown" for Logged-In User <span class="done-tag">✅</span></h4>
  <p>User is logged in as "mark" but session awards panel shows "Unknown" for that participant.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Investigate where the display name is resolved for awards — likely the connection is not yet associated with the user profile at the time the award is rendered</li>
    <li>Ensure <code>participantName</code> (or equivalent) is populated before any award or leaderboard render, not just after the first vote</li>
    <li>Add a fallback: if a name resolves to null/empty/undefined, use the stored <code>es_displayName</code> from localStorage</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>T3 — Ocean Week: Shark and Fish Swim the Wrong Way by Default <span class="done-tag">✅</span></h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Shark and fish runners in Ocean Week enter from the wrong side — they should enter from the left and swim right by default, matching natural reading direction</li>
    <li>Fix the default <code>direction</code> and/or <code>scaleX</code> in <code>seasonal.js</code> for the Ocean Week shark and fish animation entries</li>
    <li>This is a config fix only — no new UI required (configurable direction is tracked separately in AA6)</li>
    <li>File: <code>wwwroot/js/seasonal.js</code></li>
  </ul>

  <h4>T4 — Floor Is Lava Test Doesn't Toggle to Stop (Just Resets) <span class="done-tag">✅</span></h4>
  <p>The 🧪 Test button for Floor Is Lava does not change to a "Stop" button while the test is running — clicking it again just restarts instead of stopping. (S1 was planned but the stop toggle was not fully implemented.)</p>
